<h1>Privacy policy</h1>
<p class="muted">Last updated: <%- legal('lastUpdated') %></p>

<p>This policy explains which personal data Signoff processes, why, for how long, with whom, and what your rights are. It applies the General Data Protection Regulation (GDPR, Regulation (EU) 2016/679) and the Belgian Act of 30 July 2018 on the protection of natural persons with regard to the processing of personal data.</p>

<h2>1. Who is responsible for your data?</h2>
<table>
  <tbody>
    <tr><th scope="row">Publisher of the service</th><td><%- legal('companyName') %> (<%- legal('legalForm') %>)</td></tr>
    <tr><th scope="row">Registered office</th><td><%- legal('address') %></td></tr>
    <tr><th scope="row">Enterprise number (BCE/KBO)</th><td><%- legal('enterpriseNumber') %></td></tr>
    <tr><th scope="row">VAT number</th><td><%- legal('vatNumber') %></td></tr>
    <tr><th scope="row">Contact email</th><td><%- legal('contactEmail') %></td></tr>
    <tr><th scope="row">Legal representative</th><td><%- legal('legalRepresentative') %></td></tr>
  </tbody>
</table>
<p>Signoff is an online service that lets a freelancer have their client approve deliverables or project stages (called "milestones" or "deliveries" depending on the activity), with a timestamped history.</p>
<p>There are two situations:</p>
<ul>
  <li><strong>Your account data</strong> (if you are a freelancer): Signoff is the <strong>controller</strong>.</li>
  <li><strong>Your clients' data</strong> that you enter or send in Signoff (name, email, files, comments): you are the controller, Signoff acts as <strong>processor</strong> and only uses this data to provide the service, under the data processing agreement in the <a href="/terms#dpa">terms of use</a>.</li>
</ul>

<h2>2. What data, why, and on what basis?</h2>
<table>
  <thead><tr><th>Data</th><th>Purpose</th><th>Legal basis (Art. 6 GDPR)</th></tr></thead>
  <tbody>
    <tr><td>Freelancer account: first name, last name, name shown to your clients (name or business name), email, password (stored only as a hash, never in plain text), language, activity and answers to the welcome questionnaire<% if (beta) { %>, date the beta rules were accepted (<code>beta_rules_accepted_at</code>)<% } %></td><td>Create and secure the account, provide the service</td><td>Performance of the contract (Art. 6(1)(b))</td></tr>
    <tr><td>Content of your projects: projects, milestones or deliveries, amounts, deliverables (links, texts), project frame, supplements</td><td>Provide the service</td><td>Performance of the contract (Art. 6(1)(b))</td></tr>
    <tr><td>Client data entered by the freelancer: name, email, project name</td><td>Let the client open the approval page and approve</td><td>Performance of the contract / legitimate interest of the freelancer, who is the controller (Art. 6(1)(b) and (f))</td></tr>
    <tr><td>Uploaded files and the SHA-256 fingerprint of each file</td><td>Deliver the file to the client and show it was not changed after approval</td><td>Performance of the contract (Art. 6(1)(b))</td></tr>
    <tr><td>Event log: opening of the link, acceptance of the frame, approval, change request and its comments (including file references such as "/file1", with the list of files in the order the client saw them), answers to supplements; full name typed by the client when approving; date and time (UTC), IP address and browser (user agent) of the client at each action; frozen copy of the deliverables at the moment of approval</td><td>Build the timestamped history of the approval, an element of proof for the freelancer</td><td>Legitimate interest (proof) / performance of the contract (Art. 6(1)(f) and (b))</td></tr>
    <tr><td>Freelancer's private notes</td><td>The freelancer's own use, never shown to the client</td><td>Performance of the contract (Art. 6(1)(b))</td></tr>
    <tr><td>Password reset requests (only a fingerprint of the link is kept)</td><td>Let you choose a new password</td><td>Performance of the contract (Art. 6(1)(b))</td></tr>
    <tr><td>Support and feedback messages sent through the "<%= t('feedback.link') %>" link (the beta's Discord server) or to the contact address: username or address, content of the message</td><td>Answer questions, fix bugs, improve the service</td><td>Legitimate interest / consent of the person writing (Art. 6(1)(f) and (a))</td></tr>
    <tr><td>Session cookie (signed, 30 days) and security token against forged forms (CSRF)</td><td>Keep you signed in, remember the language, protect forms</td><td>Strictly necessary: no consent required</td></tr>
    <tr><td>Server technical logs (errors, requests, IP address)</td><td>Security, troubleshooting</td><td>Legitimate interest (Art. 6(1)(f))</td></tr>
  </tbody>
</table>
<p>While sending emails is not turned on, the content of notification emails (password reset links included) is written to the server's technical logs instead of being sent.</p>
<p>We use no advertising cookies, no audience measurement and no third-party trackers. Fonts are served by the app itself. We do not sell your data. We make no automated decisions about you.</p>

<h2>3. Who is it shared with (processors)?</h2>
<table>
  <thead><tr><th>Provider</th><th>Role</th><th>Location</th></tr></thead>
  <tbody>
    <tr><td>Render</td><td>Hosting of the application</td><td><%- legal('regionRender') %></td></tr>
    <tr><td>Neon</td><td>PostgreSQL database</td><td><%- legal('regionNeon') %></td></tr>
    <tr><td>Cloudflare R2</td><td>Storage of uploaded files, and storage of the database backups (in a separate space)</td><td><%- legal('regionR2') %></td></tr>
    <tr><td>GitHub (Actions)</td><td>Runs the automatic database backup every night: the copy is made on a GitHub machine, then sent to Cloudflare R2</td><td><%- legal('regionGitHub') %></td></tr>
    <tr><td>Resend</td><td>Sending emails (notifications, deadline reminders, password reset), when sending emails is turned on</td><td><%- legal('regionResend') %></td></tr>
    <tr><td>Discord</td><td>The beta community: support and feedback from testers (a service used outside the app, under its own privacy policy)</td><td><%- legal('regionDiscord') %></td></tr>
  </tbody>
</table>
<p>No payment provider is used at this time.</p>
<p>When a provider processes data outside the European Economic Area, the transfer is covered by the European Commission's standard contractual clauses or by an adequacy decision (including the EU–US Data Privacy Framework for certified providers).</p>
<p>The freelancer sees the data of their own projects. The client only sees the milestone or delivery whose link they received.</p>

<h2>4. How long do we keep it?</h2>
<ul>
  <li><strong>Account and project data</strong>: as long as the account exists. A project, milestone or delivery you delete is erased from the database at once, with its history.</li>
  <li><strong>Account deletion</strong> (by yourself from "My profile", or by an administrator on written request): the account, the projects, the milestones or deliveries with their deliverables, the files, the frames and their acceptances, the notes, the supplements, the event logs and the password reset requests are erased from the database in a single operation, even if a delivery was already approved and locked. Links sent to clients stop working.</li>
  <li><strong>Files in storage</strong>: they are erased right after the account. If the storage does not answer, or if the deletion is done by an administrator without access to it, the remaining files are put on a waiting list (table <code>storage_orphans</code>) and then erased by the cleanup command <code>admin:clean-storage</code>, within <%- legal('storageCleanupDays') %> of the account deletion.</li>
  <li><strong>Backups</strong>: a full copy of the database is made every night. Deleted data may remain in backups until they expire, that is <%- legal('backupRetentionDays') %>, and is then erased.</li>
  <li><strong>Inactive accounts</strong>: time before deletion: <%- legal('inactiveAccountMonths') %>. This deletion is not automatic at this time: an administrator does it.</li>
  <li><strong>Password reset links</strong>: valid for 1 hour (24 hours when an administrator creates them), usable once.</li>
  <li><strong>Billing data</strong> (once payments exist): <%- legal('billingRetentionYears') %>.</li>
  <li><strong>Technical logs</strong>: according to the host's retention period.</li>
</ul>

<h2>5. Your rights</h2>
<p>You can ask for access to your data, its rectification, its erasure, restriction of processing, portability, and object to processing based on legitimate interest. Write to <%- legal('contactEmail') %><% if (feedback) { %> (or through the app's "<%= t('feedback.link') %>" link)<% } %>; we answer within one month. Proof of identity may be requested in case of doubt. You can also delete your account yourself from "My profile".</p>
<p><strong>Are you a freelancer's client?</strong> First contact the freelancer who sent you the link (the controller); we will help them answer.</p>
<p>If you believe your rights are not respected, you can lodge a complaint with the Belgian supervisory authority:</p>
<p>
  <strong>Data Protection Authority (Autorité de protection des données)</strong><br>
  Rue de la Presse 35, 1000 Brussels<br>
  Phone: +32 (0)2 274 48 00<br>
  Email: <a href="mailto:contact@apd-gba.be">contact@apd-gba.be</a><br>
  Website: <a href="https://www.dataprotectionauthority.be" target="_blank" rel="noopener">www.dataprotectionauthority.be</a>
</p>

<h2>6. Security</h2>
<p>Hashed passwords, password reset links stored as a fingerprint, encrypted connection (HTTPS), protection against forged forms (CSRF), rate limiting, security headers, access control on every resource, database lock on approved milestones and deliveries, automatic backups every night. No system is infallible: in the event of a data breach likely to harm you, we notify the Data Protection Authority and the people concerned within the legal deadlines (72 hours for the authority).</p>

<% if (beta) { %>
<h2>7. Test beta</h2>
<p>During the beta, the service is meant for testing: do not send any real client data. Beta accounts and data may be deleted at any time. When signing up, you accept the beta rules (checkbox); the date of this acceptance is recorded. Person responsible for the beta: <%- legal('betaResponsible') %>.</p>
<p>During the beta, if sending emails is not turned on, a forgotten password is reset by an administrator, who sends you a link valid for 24 hours.</p>
<% } %>

<h2><%= beta ? '8' : '7' %>. Changes</h2>
<p>This policy may change, especially when the beta ends; the date of the last update is at the top of the page. Last updated: <%- legal('lastUpdated') %>.</p>
